## 📦 Installation Guide

### 1. Virtual Machine Setup

**Prerequisites:**
- VirtualBox 7.2.8+ installed
- 16GB+ host RAM recommended
- 100GB+ free disk space

**Network Configuration (Host-Only Adapter):**
| VM | IP Address |
|----|------------|
| Ubuntu (ELK) | 192.168.56.10 |
| Windows 10 | 192.168.56.20 |
| Kali | 192.168.56.30 |

### 2. ELK Stack Installation on Ubuntu

```bash
# Install prerequisites
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install apt-transport-https zip unzip lsb-release curl gnupg -y

# Add Elastic repository
wget -qO - https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/elasticsearch-keyring.gpg
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/elasticsearch-keyring.gpg] https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/8.x/apt stable main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/elastic-8.x.list


Configure Elasticsearch (/etc/elasticsearch/elasticsearch.yml):
# Install components
sudo apt update
sudo apt install elasticsearch kibana logstash -y
network.host: 192.168.56.10
http.port: 9200
discovery.type: single-node
xpack.security.enabled: false


Set JVM Heap Size (/etc/elasticsearch/jvm.options.d/heap.options):
-Xms1g
-Xmx1g

Configure Kibana (/etc/kibana/kibana.yml):
server.host: "0.0.0.0"
elasticsearch.hosts: ["http://192.168.56.10:9200"]

Configure Logstash (/etc/logstash/conf.d/winlogbeat.conf):
input {
  beats {
    port => 5044
    host => '0.0.0.0'
  }
}
output {
  elasticsearch {
    hosts => ['http://192.168.56.10:9200']
    index => 'winlogbeat-%{+YYYY.MM.dd}'
    ssl_certificate_verification => false
  }
}

Start services:
sudo systemctl start elasticsearch
sudo systemctl enable elasticsearch
sudo systemctl start kibana
sudo systemctl enable kibana
sudo systemctl start logstash
sudo systemctl enable logstash


3. Windows Endpoint Setup
Install Sysmon:
# Download Sysmon and config
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SwiftOnSecurity/sysmon-config/main/sysmonconfig.xml" -OutFile "sysmonconfig.xml"

# Install Sysmon
.\Sysmon64.exe -accepteula -i .\sysmonconfig.xml

Install and Configure Winlogbeat:
# Download Winlogbeat (from elastic.co)

# Edit winlogbeat.yml
# Set output.logstash.hosts: ["192.168.56.10:5044"]

# Add Sysmon log source
winlogbeat.event_logs:
  - name: Application
  - name: Security
  - name: System
  - name: Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational

# Install and start service
.\install-service-winlogbeat.ps1
Start-Service winlogbeat

4. Kali Attack Machine
sudo apt update
sudo apt install hydra nmap -y

🚨 Detection Capabilities
Attack Type	Detection Method	Windows Event ID	MITRE Technique
Brute Force	Failed login threshold	4625	T1110.001
Network Recon	Port scan detection	5156	T1046

Custom Detection Rule (Kibana)
# Brute Force Detection (10+ failed attempts in 5 minutes)
event.code: 4625
| stats count by source.ip, winlog.event_data.TargetUserName
| where count > 10

⚔️ Attack Simulation & Results
Simulated Attack 1: SMB Brute Force (Hydra)
Kali Command:
hydra -l administrator -P /tmp/passwords.txt smb://192.168.56.20 -t 1
Generated Events:
10 failed login attempts (Event ID 4625)
Source IP: 192.168.56.30
Target: 192.168.56.20

Simulated Attack 2: Network Reconnaissance (Nmap)
Kali Command:
nmap -sS 192.168.56.20

Generated Events:
Port scan detected (Event ID 5156)
20+ port probes logged



